09,"output_tokens":1872,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"f889a5abbf256867d067d0ff05feb65dc3e232638a8ab1af033a7832cf661fec"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":57558,"output_tokens":2361,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Gate the real-grandchild reaping test in tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py behind an explicit POSIX-only skip (mirroring the `os.name == 'posix'` spawn guard), since `sleep`/process-group reaping do not exist on the Windows harness cell.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1222,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"a real child that forks a `sleep 30` grandchild is spawned, the timeout forced, and afterwards `os.kill(pid, 0)` raises `ProcessLookupError` for both pids\"","step 2 guards spawn with `start_new_session=(os.name == \"posix\")`, acknowledging non-POSIX differs","`sleep` is not a Windows binary; Windows lacks POSIX process groups and `os.kill(pid, 0)` signal-0 probe semantics"],"finding":"The new grandchild-reaping test spawns a real child that forks a `sleep 30` grandchild and asserts `os.kill(pid, 0)` raises `ProcessLookupError` for both pids. Both `sleep` and POSIX `os.kill(pid, 0)` / process-group semantics are POSIX-only, but the plan guards `start_new_session` for POSIX (`os.name == 'posix'`) yet does not state a corresponding platform skip for this test. `make verify` is part of the supported harness and runs on Windows.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9f6debffb8ca63e3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 6 / tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py","norm_id":"n7c93bcd4577404ed","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-adv